# cellar_play.log — a save, in the only form this engine has one.
#
# DESIGN.md §12: a save is (engine-hash, game-hash, ACTION LOG). Not a state
# dump — state written outside the log is state replay cannot reproduce, which
# forfeits shareable playthroughs, branching and time travel in one move. So a
# playthrough is exactly this: the world it was played against, then one line
# per tick naming the orders submitted in that tick (space-separated; a blank
# line is a tick that changed nothing).
#
# This particular log is the cellar solved: fetch the torch from the hall
# (nothing can be picked up in the dark cellar without it), then the key, then
# the lock — and the guard for the shoulder the poisoned hero does not have. It is also the fixture two
# different clients are held to: `web/platform_check.mjs` plays the cart by
# CLICKING and asserts the log it produced is this file, and
# `tests/test_secondclient.c` replays this file through `world_*` alone and
# asserts it lands in the same world. Neither client can be quietly special —
# they meet here.

story examples/cellar_play.story

go_hall(hero)
take(hero,torch,hall)
go_cellar(hero)
take(hero,rusty_key,cellar)
go_hall(hero)
unlock(hero)
force_door(guard)
enter_vault(hero)
take(hero,antidote,vault)
drink(hero)
